{"kind":"request","text":"NF-8: two follow-ups from the NF-5 review b6e9f538.\n\n1. The `locked` answer at the send step. Since NF-5, each delivery\n   enters the store's `exclusive` section. The Node file store takes\n   the `capacity.lease` lock there and throws\n   `CustodyError({held:\"locked\"})` after `LEASE_WAIT_MS` of\n   contention. The record is then marked `sent`, and nothing was\n   delivered. The gate covers this path with no contention only.\n   Add one named case: two processes contend for one file store, one\n   send answers `locked`, and the existing recovery then sends the\n   same bytes one time. State in `docs/cli.md` and `docs/mcp.md` what\n   a caller sees and does. Change no lock rule unless the case shows\n   a lost or doubled send, and stop for the planner in that case.\n\n2. The sentence \"Nothing was sent.\" of RETIRED_REQUEST. For a\n   version 1 join slot or a Counter record in the phase `sent` or\n   `unknown`, an envelope can have left before the cutover. The\n   sentence can then be false. Replace it with words that are true in\n   each case, for example \"This page sent nothing now\", or remove it.\n   Request c288c917 asks only that the page says the room retired.\n\nThis request adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no\ncapability name or form, no tool family and no record model. It is a\nside lane. It takes no gate position before C3, the tooling head and\nE1, and it can ride NF-6.","body":{"conditions":"One named case shows the locked answer under contention and one later send of the same bytes. The two documents state what a caller sees. No page says that nothing was sent when an envelope can have left. The gate passes.","target_head":"26d1e65cd9a6815abc70c832f1e61b893bb8b689","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}